error[L0515]: `bump!` changes its argument, but this call passes it a copy
  --> check/changing_function_value.knv:10:15
   |
 4 | (defn bump! (x) (set! x (+ x 1)))
   |                 ---------------- this would change only the copy
...
10 |   (take-value bump! total)
   |               ^^^^^ this parameter expects `int`, and `bump!` takes `(mut int)`
   |
   = help: to change a copy on purpose, write `(type bump! (fn (int) unit))`, or wrap the body in `(let (x x) ...)`
   = note: run `knave doc L0515` for an explanation

error[L0515]: `bump!` changes its argument, but the field `apply` passes it a copy
  --> check/changing_function_value.knv:11:33
   |
 4 | (defn bump! (x) (set! x (+ x 1)))
   |                 ---------------- this would change only the copy
...
11 |   (local next (new step (:apply bump!)))
   |                                 ^^^^^ the function in `apply` expects `int`, and `bump!` takes `(mut int)`
   |
   = help: to change a copy on purpose, write `(type bump! (fn (int) unit))`, or wrap the body in `(let (x x) ...)`
   = note: run `knave doc L0515` for an explanation

